# tourist-web environment variables — NAMES ONLY. Never commit real values.

# --- Public map data source (server-side, checkpoint 1B.9) ---
# Base URL of the admin-web deployment whose public read API
# (GET /api/public/maps/{mapId}) this app fetches published map snapshots
# from. Server-only — read exclusively by the Server Component at
# app/maps/[mapId]/page.tsx (lib/public-map/public-map-client.ts), never sent
# to the browser, so it is deliberately NOT NEXT_PUBLIC_. Defaults to
# http://localhost:3000 (admin-web's normal `pnpm dev` port) when unset, so
# local development works out of the box without creating a .env.local first
# — see public-map-client.ts's own doc comment.
ADMIN_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# --- Google Maps rendering (browser, NEXT_PUBLIC_ — checkpoint 1B.9) ---
# Google Maps JavaScript API key for the public tourist map
# (components/public-map/tourist-map.tsx). Not secret by design (restricted
# via HTTP-referrer/API restrictions in the Google Cloud Console, not by
# hiding the string) — same reasoning as admin-web's own
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY. A separate BROWSER key from admin-web's,
# and never the server-only Google Places credential
# (GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY) — that key is billable per-request and must never
# reach a browser. Deliberately left UNSET for local dev/E2E: with no key
# configured, the map falls back to a friendly "Map preview is unavailable"
# state instead of crashing — see components/public-map/tourist-map.tsx.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=YOUR_REAL_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY
